# Final Master Implementation Plan — Hi-Profile Bento Grid Spatial Editor

Stabilize and elevate the existing Hi-Profile Bento page into a spatial, production-grade grid editor. The mathematical **Grid Engine** is the highest-priority foundation: all layout interactions (drag, 8-handle resize, placement, collision reflow, vertical compaction, breakpoint column clamping) will be mathematically sound before building the interaction layer and visual polish.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Grid Engine Highest Priority**: All layout operations (placement, drag, 8-handle resize, collision pushing, vertical compaction, responsive column clamping) operate on the mathematical layout state `{ x, y, w, h }` as the single source of truth.
> - **Responsive Layout Clamping (4 / 2 / 1 Columns)**: When breakpoint changes (Desktop 4 cols → Tablet 2 cols → Mobile 1 col), block widths and positions are dynamically clamped (`w = Math.min(w, activeCols)`, `x = Math.min(x, activeCols - w)`), resolved for collisions, and vertically compacted.
> - **Strict 10 Block Types**: `Emoji`, `Link`, `Text`, `Checklist`, `Image`, `Instagram`, `GitHub`, `YouTube`, `Twitter/X`, and `LinkedIn`. No unsupported block types or external widgets will be added.
> - **No Drag/Resize API Spam**: Pointer interactions modify local layout state in real-time. Persistence is debounced by 800ms after the pointer settles, maintaining high UI frame rates.

